# Market Context

> Cited, verifiable facts the writing skills draw on when a post or comment needs data.
> `/post` and `/commenting-others` read this file.
>
> **An empty table is a valid state.** The skills write without stats when there are none.
> Never let a skill invent a number to fill this file.
>
> Every row needs a real source and the date you checked it. A statistic with no source is
> worse than no statistic, and in a regulated field it is a compliance breach.

| Fact | Number | Source (name + link) | As at |
|------|--------|----------------------|-------|
| [ xxx ] | [ xxx ] | [ xxx ] | [ xxx ] |

## Notes

- Prefer a primary source over a summary of one.
- Re-check anything older than 12 months before using it again.
- If a number cannot be sourced, cut it from the draft rather than softening it into
  "studies show" or "research suggests" (both banned in `.claude/rules/anti-ai.md`).
